{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>These too are the proverbs of Solomon</b> — this verse the scribe said. And it is possible that it was Shebnah, for he was the king's scribe, and he recorded in it the reason for the copying." "<b>Also</b> — to include the earlier ones." "<b>They copied</b> — he gave orders to copy these proverbs from his books so as to be one collection, and the beginning of this section was 'the glory of Elohim.'"], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra alludes to 2 Kings 18:18, where Shebnah is designated 'the scribe'; identity of the scribe of Proverbs 25:1 inferred by context."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:24:35.865525817Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}